#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:6
msgid "Limits of Trait Objects"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:9
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:10
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:19
msgid "// 4 bytes, owned value\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:20
msgid "// 8 bytes, reference\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:21
msgid "// 16 bytes, wide pointer\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:27
msgid "Trait objects are a limited way of solving problems."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:29
msgid ""
"If you want to downcast to a concrete type from a trait object, you will "
"need to specify that the trait in question has Any as a supertrait or that "
"the trait object is over the main trait and `Any`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:33
msgid "Even then, you will still need to cast a `dyn MyTrait` to `dyn Any`"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:35
msgid ""
"Trait objects have overhead in memory, they are \"wide pointers\" that need "
"to hold not just the pointer to the data itself but another pointer for the "
"vtable."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:39
msgid ""
"Trait objects, being dynamically sized types, can only be used practically "
"via reference or pointer types."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/limits.md:42
msgid ""
"There is a baseline overhead of dereferencing the value and relevant trait "
"methods when using trait objects."
msgstr ""
